Find out container IP address: docker inspect -f '{{range .NetworkSettings.Networks}}{{.IPAddress}}{{end}}' container_name

List out docker networks: docker network ls

Find out particular container network name: docker inspect container_name | grep "NetworkMode"

Find out list of funing containers: docker ps

Find out list of all containers: docker ps -a

Find out container logs: docker logs container_name

Check Environment Variables Inside Container: docker exec -it container_name env | grep PGADMIN

Stop container: docker stop container_name

Remove container: docker rm container_name

Restart container: docker restart container_name

Start or run any container with username and password set: docker run -p 5050:80 \
  -e PGADMIN_DEFAULT_EMAIL=admin@example.com \
  -e PGADMIN_DEFAULT_PASSWORD=admin123 \
  --name pgadmin4 \
  -d dpage/pgadmin4




  
